      "rule": "R19",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "Lake’s `input_dir` hashes file contents in path order but omits the paths from the hash, so renaming its only SQL file can leave the trace unchanged and let Lake reuse a module whose recorded SQL path no longer exists. Fix: Require a binary `input_file` for each consumed path or compare the compiled byte hash with the file at that path."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261122T125335Z-77135ee2#2",
      "line": 167,
      "path": "docs/records/spec-lean-code-store.md",
      "rule": "R19",
      "severity": "should",
      "text": "The file-key description still says that reading an external input makes the key change, although changing only the final SQL line ending can leave every hashed build product identical. Fix: State that an SQL edit changes the key through the build products only if at least one product changes."
    }
